# shared/link — core<->head link frame codec (B-link)

Header-only, Arduino-free frame codec: `link_codec.h` (namespace `link`).
Normative wire source: `link_codec.h` itself.

## Frame layout

All multi-byte fields big-endian. Total = 10 + payload bytes.

| Offset | Size | Field   | Meaning                                                  |
| ------ | ---- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| 0      | 1    | magic   | `0x4C` (`'L'`, `kMagic`) — frame sync byte               |
| 1      | 1    | type    | Frame type (see type table)                              |
| 2..3   | 2    | seq     | Sequence number `u16BE` (`isFreshSeq` wrap-aware check)   |
| 4..5   | 2    | frag    | Fragment locator `u16BE`: **idx hi, total lo**           |
| 6..7   | 2    | len     | Payload length `u16BE` (0..1024)                         |
| 8..    | len  | payload | Type-defined bytes                                       |
| 8+len  | 2    | CRC16   | CRC16-CCITT-FALSE (`poly 0x1021, init 0xFFFF`) `u16BE` over all preceding bytes |

Frag packing, exactly: `frag = (idx << 8) | total`. Unfragmented frames
use `idx=0, total=1`. `fragTotal` is a `u8` (max 255 fragments); a payload
needing more fragments must use larger per-frame payloads (up to 1024B).

`decodeFrame` validates magic, exact length, frag bounds, the per-type length
contract, then CRC. Unknown types are rejected (frozen contract).

## Type table

| Type   | Name     | Dir         | Payload (exact length, BE multi-byte)              |
| ------ | -------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| `0x01` | FACE     | core->head  | Face id `u8` (1B; clamped downstream, not here)    |
| `0x02` | OLED     | core->head  | Mode `u8` (1B): 0=ON 1=DIM 2=OFF                   |
| `0x03` | CAMCTL   | core->head  | Camera `u8` (1B): 0=off 1=on                      |
| `0x04` | — | RETIRED (was QRBITMAP, never sent; do not reuse) | — |
| `0x05` | OTA      | core->head  | OTA pull URL bytes, no NUL (1..128B)               |
| `0x06` | PAIRSHOW | core->head  | 6 ASCII digits + valid-seconds `u16BE` (8B)        |
| `0x07` | PAIRDONE | core->head  | Empty (0B; the frame presence is the signal)       |
| `0x10` | JPEG     | head->core  | Raw JPEG bytes (0..1024B; stills over TCP)         |
| `0x20` | HB       | head->core  | `rssi i8` + `channel u8` + `freeHeap u32BE` + `bootId u32BE` (10B) |
| `0x21` | HB_ACK   | core->head  | `channel u8` + `era/resync u32BE` (5B)              |
| `0x22` | ACK      | either      | Acked seq `u16BE` (2B)                             |

### Boot epoch + seq resync rule (normative)

`bootId` is a per-boot random `u32` in every HB. The core accepts any seq on
a changed-or-first-seen epoch, then gates strictly-greater within one epoch.

## Pairing-screen contract (normative)

The core sends the 6 digits + validity window and the head renders them, so
no bitmap rides the wire. Types `0x06`/`0x07` are additive; `0x04` stays
frozen and is never reused.

### PAIRSHOW (`0x06`, core->head, exactly 8B)

| Offset | Size | Field       | Meaning                                              |
| ------ | ---- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| 0..5   | 6    | digits      | 6 ASCII digits `'0'`..`'9'`                          |
| 6..7   | 2    | valid-secs  | Validity window `u16BE` (0 = already-expired display) |

The digit vocabulary is validated fail-closed both ways by
`packPairShow`/`unpackPairShow` (non-digit rejects); the frame codec
checks the 8B length only, never values.

### PAIRDONE (`0x07`, core->head, empty)

No payload — the frame presence is the signal. The contract is
fixed-empty (not a 0..N range), so any stowaway byte fails the decode
gate.

## MTU / fragmentation rule

Max single-frame payload: **1024B** (`kMaxPayload`, frame 1034B). A
transport may impose a smaller MTU later; per-frame payloads must then
shrink — the codec reports the need, the transport does the splitting:

- `maxPayloadFor(mtu)` — largest payload fitting `mtu` (0 when even
  header+CRC do not fit).
- `needsFrag(payloadLen, mtu)` — true when the payload needs splitting.
- `fragCount(payloadLen, mtu)` — frame count for the split.
- `Reassembler` — strict in-order append into a caller buffer:
  duplicates, gaps/out-of-order, total mismatches, and overflows are
  rejected without mutating state.

## Non-reuse + transport statements (normative)

- Phone-wire headers `0xAA`/`0xBB`/`0x50`/`0x51`/`0x52`/`0xAC`/`0xAD`/
  `0x53`/`0x54`/`0x55`/`0x56` are **never reused or renumbered** on the
  link wire. The link magic `0x4C` is disjoint from all of them, and link
  type bytes live at offset 1 — no phone-wire parser can accept a link
  frame and vice versa. Pinned by
  `test_link_phone_wire_headers_distinct`.
- **ESP-NOW is NOT a transport for this codec — sockets only.** This codec
  only frames bytes.
